# Lean 4 compiled objects + formal proof/build outputs (rebuild:
# `pixi run prooflib` / `tools/proof.sh <stem>` / `fire.py formalbuild`)
*.olean
*.olean.srcsha256
# The flock file `formal.lean.ensure_library` takes while building an .olean.
# Never meaningful between runs, and it must NOT be gitignored as a pattern
# that would also swallow a real build product — hence the explicit name.
*.olean.buildlock
/output/
# `fire.py build --formal` writes <stem>_proof.lean next to the source, the
# same place it writes <stem>.aout (gitignored above). test_formal.py instead
# keeps artifacts under output/, so a proof built by hand lands in the tree
# untracked; these are rebuildable from the source, not sources themselves.
*_proof.lean
